.TITLE "cp"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Copies files and directories. It creates a duplicate of the __source__ at the specified __destination__ and is the primary tool for file duplication on macOS.

.DIV "TLDR"
**cp source.txt destination.txt**
Copies a single file to a new location or filename.
> __source.txt__ the original file | __destination.txt__ the new copy

**cp -R source_dir destination_dir**
Copies an entire directory and all its contents recursively.
> __-R__ recursive flag | __source_dir__ original directory | __destination_dir__ target directory

**cp -p source.txt destination.txt**
Preserves the original file's modification time, access time, and permissions.
> __-p__ preserve flag

**cp -v source.txt destination.txt**
Displays the name of each file as it is being copied.
> __-v__ verbose flag

**cp -n source.txt destination.txt**
Prevents overwriting an existing file at the destination.
> __-n__ no-clobber flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
On macOS, using the __-R__ flag is preferred over __-r__ for recursive copies to ensure proper handling of symbolic links and special files. Use __-i__ if you want to be prompted before overwriting files.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:mv** **mac:rm**

